    "title": "L1 m=4, h=3, nu=0, h=0 universal packet exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "The universal normalized constant-eliminant packet (a/R(0)^2,b/R(0)^3)=(6,20) is impossible: its Euler identity makes X^n(R-4R(0))/(D(R-R(0))^4) a pth power, but the forced root multiplicities cannot sum to deg(R-R(0))=p. Thus the h=0 nonzero-b endpoint is empty on the first three official characteristics; only the exceptional largest-characteristic packet remains.",
